{
  "A panel that slides in from an edge of the page or a container, either over the content or pushing it aside. Users can swipe it in from the edge and back out, and Escape, the scrim and the browser's back action close it.": "",
  "Page-level drawer": "",
  "Bind it with `x-model`, or open it with `open()` and `show(host)` as with a bottom sheet. Over the page, it opens in the top layer as a modal with a scrim.": "",
  "Edges, push mode and swipe gestures": "",
  "This example opens over a frame (`container`) from any edge. `push` moves the frame's content aside (`pushTarget`) and is not modal unless requested. With `edgeSwipe`, a finger on a touch screen opens it from the edge. Every option can be changed live.": "",
  "Touch and keyboard": "",
  "The drawer follows the finger. Releasing past half its size, or flicking it, leaves it open. Otherwise, it slides back.": "",
  "It follows the finger. Releasing past halfway, or flicking it, closes it. A swipe on content that scrolls horizontally goes to that content.": "",
  "It closes, and each of these has an option.": "",
  "The panel has `role=\"dialog\"` and is named by its title, `label` or \"Side panel\". It has `aria-modal` when modal, and the surrounding content is `inert`.": "",
  "Moves in when it opens as a modal, and returns to where it was when it closes.": "",
  "`start` is the left edge in left-to-right pages and the right edge in right-to-left pages, and the animation follows.": "",
  "Its default name and the close button come from `uiLocale.strings` (`drawerLabel`, `close`).": "Varsayılan adı ve kapatma düğmesi `uiLocale.strings` değerinden gelir (`drawerLabel`, `close`).",
  "The layer. `data-side` (`start`, `end`, `top`, `bottom`), `data-mode`, `data-open`, `data-modal`, `data-scrim`, `data-contained`, `data-dragging`.": "Katman. `data-side` (`start`, `end`, `top`, `bottom`), `data-mode`, `data-open`, `data-modal`, `data-scrim`, `data-contained`, `data-dragging`.",
  "The dialog. `--_size`, plus `--_shift-x` and `--_shift-y` during a drag.": "",
  "The element a push drawer moves aside, using `--_mx-push`.": "",
  "Units: the dimmed layer, the surface at each edge (`start`, `end`, `top`, `bottom`, which differ in the sides facing the content and the available space), and the surface when pushing content (`push`).": "",
  "The opening size, the maximum share of the available space, the margin around it, and the font family.": "",
  "The edge it slides in from. `start` and `end` follow the reading direction, and `left` and `right` do not.": "",
  "Over the content, or pushing `pushTarget` aside by its size.": "",
  "The element `push` moves aside. Without it, `push` behaves like `over`.": "",
  "Its width, or its height from the top or bottom, in pixels or as a CSS length. `null` uses `drawer.size`. It never exceeds 85% of the available space.": "",
  "A finger swiping in from the edge of the container or page opens it, and it follows the finger.": "",
  "The distance from the edge, in pixels, where that swipe can start.": "",
  "A finger swiping it back toward its edge closes it.": "",
  "A flick faster than this, in pixels per millisecond, opens or closes it regardless of distance.": "",
  "`true` for over, `false` for push": "",
  "Blocks everything around it, and Tab stays inside.": "",
  "Props shared by all overlay panels, as listed on the [BottomSheet page](/bottomsheet#api).": "",
  "Same as on a bottom sheet.": "",
  "Same as on a bottom sheet. A swipe back closes it with `reason: 'swipe'`, and an edge swipe canceled by `onOpening` does not move it.": ""
}
